<BaseLayout title="Passport Validity Checker: Expiry & Travel-Date Comparison" description="Compare passport expiry with sourced UK and Schengen date rules or your own verified destination buffer. Check the correct arrival or departure anchor."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Passport Validity Checker</h1><p class="mb-8">Compare expiry against the correct anchor date. A date comparison does not establish that you can board or enter a destination.</p><PassportValidityChecker client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Use departure for these two rules</h2><p>The UK visitor rule requires a passport valid for the full stay. Schengen’s general application guidance requires expiry at least three months beyond planned departure. Enter the date you plan to leave that destination, not the date you fly out of Pakistan.</p><h2>Other destinations</h2><p>Confirm the required validity and whether it runs from arrival or departure through the destination’s official authority and your carrier. Choose the custom mode and enter that verified anchor and buffer. There is no universal six-month rule for every nationality, destination and visa route.</p><h2>What this does not check</h2><p>Confirm passport issue-date limits, blank pages, visa validity, transit rules and identity details separately. The result only compares the dates entered, using calendar months with month-end dates clamped to the final day of the target month. It does not verify a passport’s authenticity or legal status.</p><h2>When renewal is needed</h2><p>Review our <a href="/guides/pakistan-passport-renewal/">sourced Pakistani passport renewal guide</a> for DGIP fees, online eligibility and processing uncertainty. Leave time for checks and delivery; do not rely on a promise of 24-hour urgent renewal.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
